# GitHub is the only sync target

User directive (Oct 2026): **do not sync or copy the project anywhere else — only GitHub.**

## Agents must NOT

- Run `rsync`, `scp`, `cp -R`, or similar to mirror the repo (M4 Mini, MSD card, NAS, Google Drive, second local folder, etc.).
- Restore or merge from `/Volumes/256GB MSD/Hunch` or other backup volumes unless the user explicitly asks in that message.
- Suggest or run two-way folder sync (Syncthing, Tailscale file copy) as part of finishing a task.
- Create duplicate working trees “for safety” on the same machine.

## Agents MAY

- Edit and run code in the **single** workspace: `/Users/nhharshan/Hunch`.
- Use **git** (`add`, `commit`, `push`, `pull`, `fetch`) against the configured GitHub remote when the user asks to sync or publish.
- Read GitHub (`origin`, PRs, branches) to determine remote state when the user asks.

## Commits and push

- Only commit or push when the user explicitly requests it (unchanged).
- When the user says “sync” or “back up the project,” mean **push to GitHub** (or pull from GitHub on another clone), not file copy.

## Supersedes

- Older rules that required M4 `rsync` or treated local mirrors as source of truth are **inactive** for agents; this rule wins.
